{"id": "q0450", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.61, "n_chunks": 2, "scores": [0.2643, 0.3466], "eot_score": 0.2981, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": null, "query": "When did google first start?", "transcript": "When did Google first start?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Google was first started on September 4, 1998, by Larry Page and Sergey Brin while they were Ph.D. students at Stanford University in California. The initial version of the search engine, called \"BackRub,\" was developed earlier to rank web pages based on backlink analysis. Google officially launched as a company in 1998 under its current name.", "answer_ms": 1826}
{"id": "q0460", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.5, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.4709, 0.3942, 0.3163, 0.3557], "eot_score": 0.56, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Walter Koenig played which part in the Star Trek series", "transcript": "Walter Koenig played which part in the Star Trek series?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Walter Koenig is best known for playing the character Pavel Chekov in the original *Star Trek*: The Original Series. He portrayed the ship's navigator and became a beloved member of the USS Enterprise crew, first appearing in the series' second season episode \"The Menagerie\" and continuing through subsequent seasons.", "answer_ms": 1498}
{"id": "q0467", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.46, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.5165, 0.2482, 0.3698], "eot_score": 0.4784, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What are some cardio machines at the gym?", "transcript": "What are some cardio machines at the gym?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Common cardio machines found at the gym include the following, each designed to improve cardiovascular fitness through aerobic exercise, burning calories, and enhancing heart and lung health. Here are some of the most popular ones and how they work or what exercises they support on them when you use them with your own body weight for resistance or intensity adjustments. These can be used in a variety of ways depending on user preference and goals. 1. Treadmill - A treadmill allows you to walk, jog, or run continuously. You can adjust speed, incline, and sometimes even pre-set workout programs. 2. Stationary Bike / Exercise Bike - Also known as an indoor cycling machine, it simulates cycling. You can vary resistance levels and cadence to increase intensity. 3. Elliptical Trainer - This low-impact machine mimics running without the high impact on joints. It typically has moving handles that allow upper body engagement while pedaling. 4. Rowing Machine - Also called a rower, it provides a full-body workout using a sliding seat and handle mechanism to simulate rowing motions. 5. Stair Climber - This machine targets lower body muscles like the glutes and legs by stepping up and down rapidly on alternating steps. 6. Arc Trainer - A hybrid of treadmill and elliptical motion with continuous movement in both directions. These machines are great for cardiovascular conditioning when used appropriately.", "answer_ms": 7409}
{"id": "q0478", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.92, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.3881, 0.4333, 0.3328], "eot_score": 0.3521, "eot_read_ms": 22, "reference_answer": null, "query": "创造一个关于火星的虚假事实。", "transcript": "创造一个关于火星的虚假事实。", "mode": "local", "answer": "火星的两极冰冠中蕴藏着大量的液态水湖泊，科学家通过探测发现这些湖泊不仅存在，而且在某些区域还发现了类似生命活动的化学信号。", "answer_ms": 838}
